{"step_index":1006,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:16:31Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T18:16:31+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T18:16:41+04:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\nWe have found the **exact source code** for that button in Centreon Web ([`listOptions.js`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266-L281)).\r\n\r\nThis reveals why `tcpdump` captured 0 packets from the backend: **The backend never makes this call.**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### The Code Behind the Buttons\r\n\r\nIn [`listOptions.js`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266-L295):\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n// 1. \"MAP Engine server address\" button:\r\nfunction testServerAddressNg() {\r\n  const urlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\"server_address_ng\"]').val();\r\n\r\n  jQuery.ajax({\r\n    type : 'GET',\r\n    url : `${urlServerNg}/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health`,\r\n    success: () => { /* Green Check */ }, \r\n    error: () => { /* Red X */ }\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\n// 2. \"MAP server address as seen by Central\" button:\r\nfunction testInternalServerAddressNg() {\r\n  const baseUrl = window.location.origin;\r\n  const internalUrlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\"internal_server_address_ng\"]').val();\r\n  const data = { url: internalUrlServerNg };\r\n\r\n  jQuery.ajax({\r\n    type: 'POST',\r\n    url: `${baseUrl}/centreon/api/latest/map/check-health`,  // <--- Sent to PHP backend!\r\n    ...\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### The Revelation\r\n\r\n1. **`MAP server address as seen by Central`** (Green check):\r\n   * Tested **server-side** by PHP on Central (`th2-centprop-be1`). It queries the internal network directly, which is why it succeeds.\r\n2. **`MAP Engine server address`** (Red X):\r\n   * Tested **client-side by your web browser** on your workstation via JavaScript AJAX!\r\n   * Your browser directly calls:\r\n     ```text\r\n     GET https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health\r\n     ```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### The 2 Exact Reasons Why Your Browser Fails\r\n\r\n#### 1. CORS Block (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)\r\n* Your browser is viewing the Centreon Web page on port **`443`** (`https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`).\r\n* The AJAX script calls port **`9443`** (`https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`).\r\n* Because the port is different (`443` vs `9443`), modern web browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge) treat this as a **Cross-Origin request**.\r\n* Browsers strictly **block** cross-origin AJAX calls unless Nginx returns CORS headers:\r\n  ```nginx\r\n  add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*' always;\r\n  add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS' always;\r\n  add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'Authorization, Content-Type' always;\r\n  ```\r\n  Without these headers, your browser silently rejects the response and displays **Connection test failed**.\r\n\r\n#### 2. Workstation Hairpin NAT\r\n* Your browser resolves `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the public IP **`109.62.64.18`**.\r\n* If your PC is connected to the internal corporate LAN/VPN, traffic from your PC targeting the corporate public VIP `109.62.64.18:9443` is dropped by the corporate firewall (lack of NAT loopback / Hairpin NAT).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### How to Verify in 5 Seconds\r\n\r\n1. On the Centreon Web page, press **F12** in your browser to open **Developer Tools**.\r\n2. Go to the **Console** tab.\r\n3. Click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\r\n4. You will see the exact red browser error, for example:\r\n   * `Access to XMLHttpRequest at 'https://map...:9443/.../health' from origin 'https://extranetclient...' has been blocked by CORS policy: No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present on the requested resource.`\r\n   * Or: `net::ERR_CONNECTION_TIMED_OUT` (Firewall dropping packet from workstati